---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Aside from "../components/Aside.astro";
import { SITE, url } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Paperling Is Free & Open Source | Apache-2.0"
  description="Explore the Paperling source code, Apache-2.0 license, contribution guide, and the story behind a no-setup Markdown editor."
  path="open-source/"
  crumbs={[{ label: "Open source", path: "open-source/" }]}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>
        Small app.
        <br />
        <em>Open notebook.</em>
      </h1>
      <p>A personal fix for a small frustration. Now open to everyone.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="article-layout">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>How it started</h2>
        <blockquote class="origin-quote">
          “I built Paperling when I was starting my journey. I kept running into
          .md files that were awkward to read, so I made something for myself to
          solve that problem.”
        </blockquote>
        <p class="subtle">— Saqlain, creator of Paperling</p>
        <h2>Free to use. Open to inspect.</h2>
        <p>
          Paperling is released under{" "}
          <a href={SITE.repo + "/blob/main/LICENSE"}>Apache-2.0</a>. You can use
          it for personal and commercial work under the license terms.
        </p>
        <h2>Useful feedback makes a difference</h2>
        <p>
          Found a bug? Include your operating system and steps to reproduce it.{" "}
          <a href={SITE.repo + "/issues"}>
            Search existing issues or open a report
          </a>
          . Keep private notes and API keys out of public reports.
        </p>
        <h2>Want to contribute?</h2>
        <p>
          Read the{" "}
          <a href={SITE.repo + "/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md"}>
            contribution guide
          </a>{" "}
          before starting. Documentation, bug reports, and fixes all help.
        </p>
        <h2>Just here to write?</h2>
        <p>
          That's welcome too. <a href={url("download/")}>Download Paperling</a>{" "}
          and give your next idea a little room.
        </p>
      </article>
      <Aside />
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
